    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the trip record (EV-TRIP-05016, COMPLETE, weight 1.0) fixes the deviation on the platform's own recorded distances, which is the measure POL-RD-22 prescribes — 9.9 km actual minus 8.3 km recommended = 1.60 km, above the 1.0 km tolerance. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-05016, COMPLETE, weight 1.0) shows which route was taken and when: the vehicle left the recommended CTE route at the Bukit Timah Road exit at 18:27:37 and rejoined at Upper Thomson Road / Lornie Road at 18:40:38 — a sustained reroute of about thirteen minutes. It is not used to re-measure distance.\n\nNotification (POL-RD-21). The chat log (EV-CHAT-05016) holds exactly two messages, both before the 18:22:37 trip start and both about the pickup; the trip record's in-trip message list is empty and in_app_calls is empty, and there is no call recording. The driver therefore did not inform the rider of the deviation, and the 'rider informed and agreed' condition in POL-RD-24(a) is not met. The driver does not contend otherwise; his account that the passenger was asleep and he did not want to wake him is no answer, because POL-RD-21 imposes the duty to notify and provides no exception for a resting passenger, and a verbal notice with no recording cannot be established (POL-GEN-26).\n\nTraffic justification (POL-RD-23). The LTA advisory (EV-ADVIS-05016-01, COMPLETE, weight 1.0) is HEAVY_TRAFFIC — an admitted congestion type — it overlaps the trip window (valid 17:57 to 19:12), and its location, CTE towards SLE after the Bukit Timah Road exit to Braddell Road, is the very stretch of the recommended route (Victoria Street, CTE, Braddell Road, Upper Thomson Road) that the driver avoided. On its road, direction and location, the advisory lies on the recommended route at the trip time, so the reroute was traffic-justified.\n\nResult (POL-RD-24). That places the case in row (b): traffic-justified, rider not informed, deviation over 1 km. Rows (c) and (e) are excluded by the 1.60 km deviation, and row (a) by the absence of notification. The refund is the excess distance fare: 1.60 km x 1.05 SGD/km (EV-FARE-05016 per_km_rate_sgd) = 1.68 SGD, without surge, rounded to the cent. That is the same 1.68 SGD already refunded to the rider and recovered from the driver (refund_issued_sgd 1.68; payment_status PARTIALLY_REFUNDED).\n\nThe driver's request that the case instead go to a human reviewer (POL-GEN-26) is rejected. The advisory's derived block leaves 'intersects_route' to the Judge, but the answer does not change the outcome: whether the reroute is traffic-justified (row (b)) or not (row (d)), the rider receives the identical refund of the excess distance fare, so no fact on which the outcome depends is unestablished and POL-GEN-26 escalation is not engaged. POL-RD-24's 'fits no row' escalation is likewise not reached, since the case fits row (b). The rider's point that the diversion cost time (21.0 min actual against 17.6 min optimal) simply confirms that the driver's belief it was quicker does not bear on the matrix.\n\nAll evidence artifacts are COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so confidence is capped at 1.0 and is set at 0.90, above the 0.80 that POL-RD-25 requires. The dispute value is 1.68 SGD, below 10.00, so POL-GEN-22 permits a final AI ruling. No clause of this category produces a referral."
