    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both parties: the platform's interim adjustment of SGD 1.68 was correct and it stands; the driver's challenge to it fails.\n\nHow the route-deviation refund matrix (POL-RD-24) applies. The deviation distance is measured the way POL-RD-22 prescribes, from the platform's recorded distances on EV-TRIP-05016: actual 9.9 km minus recommended 8.3 km = 1.60 km, above the 1.0 km tolerance (POL-RD-22), so the two no-refund 'within tolerance' rows (c) and (e) do not apply. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-05016) shows a single, clean deviation at 18:27:35 and a rejoin at 18:40:38 — a sustained reroute, not a trace artefact. The driver was never told of the change: EV-CHAT-05016 holds only the two pre-trip pickup messages (18:21:17 and 18:21:57), EV-TRIP-05016's in-trip message list and in_app_calls are empty, and there is no call recording, so POL-RD-21's notice requirement is not met, and POL-GEN-26 confirms a verbal notice with no recording cannot be established. Row (a) (traffic-justified, informed and agreed) is therefore unavailable. On traffic justification (POL-RD-23), the LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-05016-01 (COMPLETE, weight 1.0) is a HEAVY_TRAFFIC congestion type that overlaps the trip window (valid 17:57–19:12) and names the CTE towards SLE after the Bukit Timah Road exit — the recommended route's own CTE stretch before its Braddell Road exit — so the reroute is traffic-justified and row (b) applies. Even if the advisory were read as not intersecting the recommended route (its derived intersects_route is null), row (d) would apply instead; rows (b) and (d) give the same relief, so that open question changes nothing and POL-GEN-26 escalation is not engaged.\n\nThe amount. The excess distance fare is deviation 1.60 km x the per-km rate 1.05 SGD (EV-FARE-05016) = 1.68 SGD, without surge (POL-RD-24). That is exactly the sum already refunded to the rider and recovered from the driver as the interim adjustment (EV-FARE-05016 refund_issued_sgd 1.68, payment_status PARTIALLY_REFUNDED; EV-TRIP-05016 fare_adjusted event). The ruling confirms it: SGD 1.68 of the SGD 26.34 trip fare is returned to the rider.\n\nDriver, on your points: your reroute itself was legitimate — the congestion on the recommended CTE stretch justified it under POL-RD-23, and the trace shows no fare-seeking detour. But POL-RD-21 makes notification a separate duty, and the record shows none; not waking a resting passenger is not an exception the policy recognises, and a message was possible. Your 'faster for him' explanation is not borne out — recorded duration 21.0 min against the router's 17.6 min — though nothing turns on that.\n\nRider, on your points: the deviation and the absence of notice are both established, the excess distance fare is 1.68 SGD, and that refund stands.\n\nNo safety flag and no fraud flag arise, the disputed value of SGD 1.68 is below SGD 10.00, and this ruling meets the 0.80 confidence bar POL-RD-25 sets for route deviations. No clause produces a referral."
